// us.irc.inflation_adjustments — the annual Revenue Procedures in which the
// Secretary publishes the inflation-adjusted amounts of Title 26.
//
// WHY A PACKAGE. Most dollar amounts of the Code are written as a base plus
// the §1(f)(3) cost-of-living formula; the figure for a given year exists
// only in the Revenue Procedure for that year. Owners therefore left every
// indexed year outside their parameter coverage (MISSING_PARAMETER_VALUE,
// TECH-GAPS G3/G80/G81/G126/G174/G185). This package pins those publications
// once, so that every owner anchors the SAME figure on the SAME text.
//
// WHAT IT HOLDS. `sources.law` is GENERATED by
// `corpus/tools/sources/sync/sync_us_irs_revenue_procedures.py` from the IRS
// PDFs (sha256-pinned; raw bytes in the gitignored
// `docs/foundations/us-irc/raw/revproc/`): the normalized text extraction
// is the pinned publication (`sources/rp-<year>-<n>/en.txt`), and every
// numbered item of the body is one `pub fragment`
// `RP<year>_<n>_S<section>_<item>`. No rules: the value, its validity window
// and its reading belong to the owner's `.lawparam.json` row, which cites
// the fragment in `anchors`.
//
// HOW TO READ THE YEARS. Rev. Proc. 2024-40 section 2 gives the 2025 items;
// Rev. Proc. 2025-32 section 3 modifies two of them after Pub. L. 119-21
// (§63(c) standard deduction, §179) and section 4 gives the 2026 items. Its
// section 5 says which items follow taxable years and which calendar years
// — an owner reads that before choosing a validity window.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irc.inflation_adjustments version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irc:inflation_adjustments:clir";
